    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105-a1">

                <pb facs="0259" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg159"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    582.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">M. de Lesseps to Mr. Morton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Comité de l’Union Franco-Américaine</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1884-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            25, 1884</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: I have the honor to inform
                    you that agreeably to the understanding with the president of the council, we
                    have taken the necessary measures for the organization of our ceremony of
                    presentation of the statue for Friday, the 4th of July, at 11 o’clock a. m.</p>
                <p>In the name of the committee I come, therefore, to renew, officially, our
                    invitation <pb facs="0260" n="160" xml:id="pg160"/> that you kindly receive the
                    homage of the work addressed to the great American sister Republic by the
                    Franco-American Union.</p>
                <p>Please receive, &amp;c.</p>
                <p>In the name of the Franco-American Union,</p>
                <p>The president of the committee,</p>
                <closer><signed>FERD. DE LESSEPS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
